    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1="2" ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">&quot;Everyone seems to have an opinion about American black women--they need to get married, change their hair, act like &apos;ladies,&apos; and so on. Celebrated writer Tamara Winfrey Harris writes a searing account of being a black woman in America and explains why it&apos;s time for black women to speak for themselves&quot;--Provided by publisher.</marc:subfield>
